on the basic of tailwind cli

first create two folders in root folders
- dist
- src

then crete a file in dist (like index.html  it is for the last output i.e. for the production)

 then open terminal for that root folder adn run below command:
 - npx tailwindcss init
this command creates a tailwind.config.js which we need to modify after to use css

and then create a file in src folder (e.g input.css) and write below lines in input.css file (src/input.css):
@tailwind base;
@tailwind components;
@tailwind utilities;
(Note : in @tailwind will show warining lines, you can remove these lines from setting, for this open vs code setting (or ctrl + ,) and then serch unknow then choose ignore in css>lint: unknown at rules)

after then open tailwind.config.js and give your file location in content where you what to user css 
e.g for index.html
content:["./dist/index.html"]
or for all html  and js pages of dist folder
content: ["./dist/*.{html,js}"]

then run this command:
npx tailwindcss -i ./src/input.css -o ./src/output.css
(Note : -i means input file, where actual tailwind is e.g input.css and -o means output file name where we wnat to generate css e. style.css)


then link css file (style.css) with file where you want to user css
